# ---- Family: Media ----
# Tile states, and they are mutually exclusive by construction:
#   LIVE           — an endpoint is declared + probeable → clickable, probed (Homepage counts
#                    anything under 400 as up, so an edge 502 on a dead backend reads red).
#   LIVE, UNPROBED — endpoint declared, probe off: the name does not resolve from inside this
#                    container, so a dot here would be a lie. Clickable, no dot.
#   UNCONFIGURED   — no endpoint declared → non-clickable tile that says so. A service is
#                    NEVER rendered into the roadmap group: "Soon" claims not-deployed, and a
#                    live app rendered there is the bug this group exists to kill.
{% set media_url = homepage_media_url | default('') %}
{% set seerrng_url = homepage_seerrng_url | default('') %}
- Media:
    - Jellyfin:
        icon: mdi-film-roll
{% if media_url %}
        href: "{{ media_url }}"
{% if homepage_media_probe | default(true) %}
        siteMonitor: "{{ media_url }}"
        # The live answer at the root is the media server's own redirect to its web app, so the
        # expected set names it: a redirect is UP, the edge's 502-on-dead-backend is DOWN.
        status:
          code: [200, 301, 302, 307]
          description: Up / Down
{% endif %}
        description: Movies, TV & home media — streams from the home edge
{% else %}
        href: "#"
        description: Home media server — no endpoint declared
{% endif %}
    - Requests (SeerrNG):
        icon: mdi-magnify
{% if seerrng_url %}
        href: "{{ seerrng_url }}"
{% if homepage_seerrng_probe | default(false) %}
        siteMonitor: "{{ seerrng_url }}"
{% endif %}
        description: Request & track movies and series — signs in with Jellyfin
{% else %}
        href: "#"
        description: Request UI for the media server — no endpoint declared
{% endif %}

